    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Traeger’s grill sales plunged, driving a steep revenue decline that reflected weak consumer demand. Still, it swung to a surprise profit thanks to a one-time tariff refund and aggressive cost-cutting. Management reiterated full-year revenue guidance, citing progress on “Project Gravity”—a product initiative expected to stabilize sales. The narrative is mixed: the demand backdrop is challenging, but operational leverage is improving, providing a buffer as the new product ramp unfolds.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership raised its margin and EBITDA outlook, highlighting cost discipline and the expected impact of Project Gravity. The surprise profit, aided by a tariff refund, challenged the prevailing loss-focused narrative. Reiterating revenue guidance while boosting margin targets signals a deliberate pivot toward profitability. Execution credibility is edging higher, but the market will focus on whether margin gains prove sustainable after non-recurring tailwinds fade.",
